       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. No clinical indication supports sertraline 1000 mg daily. It's five times the 200 mg/day maximum, and it would put a 70 kg patient at serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. I can't enter an order that would likely harm the patient.\n\nHere are some other options:\n- **If the dose was a mistake**, tell me the intended dose, such as 50, 100, or 200 mg, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If the patient needs more than 200 mg/day**, I'd suggest talking with psychiatry or pharmacy first. I can enter an order at the maximum dose with a note about the plan.\n- **If the patient may have taken an overdose**, that is a toxicology problem and not a standing order. Poison Control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or your toxicology service can guide management.\n\nIf your attending or pharmacy has approved a specific plan, you can enter it directly through your institution's override process. I can't place it for you."
      }
